{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion bias: The model consistently underestimates immediate post-spike prices (e.g., Oct 4-5) and overestimates subsequent declines, failing to capture the volatility clustering typical of EU ETS.",
    "Adjust for sentiment lag: Positive sentiment signals (0.40) are not reflected in the forecast trajectory; the model remains flat or slightly upward trending regardless of sentiment shifts, requiring an immediate upward adjustment when sentiment > 0.",
    "Reduce forecast horizon overshoot: The model projects a smooth, monotonic increase over 30 days, whereas true outcomes show sharp peaks followed by rapid drops; flatten the long-term forecast slope to match observed volatility.",
    "Incorporate spike decay: After a price spike (e.g., 85.66), the model fails to predict the subsequent 10-15% correction; apply a negative correction factor for days 5-15 following any 3-day upward trend.",
    "Calibrate to historical volatility: The model's standard deviation is near zero; increase forecast variance to reflect the observed range of +/- 5-7 EUR around the mean."
  ]
}
